1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,547
This is the model of the river and cable problem.

2
00:00:03,497 --> 00:00:12,593
A power plant stands on one bank of a river one hundred meters wide, and the factory is five hundred meters upstream, on the opposite bank.

3
00:00:12,593 --> 00:00:22,313
The cable can first run along the bank, at ninety pesos per meter, and then cross the water diagonally, at one hundred and fifty pesos per meter.

4
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:26,329
The variable x is the stretch that runs along the bank.

5
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:34,880
Drag the orange post on the model, move the slider or the point on the graph, and watch how the two stretches and the total cost change.

6
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:43,311
The endpoint buttons take the post to x equal to zero and to x equal to five hundred, so you can compare those costs with the minimum.

7
00:00:43,311 --> 00:00:47,859
With Go to real scale you will walk through the valley at its true size.

8
00:00:47,859 --> 00:00:55,465
When you have your answer, compare it with Reveal solution, and remember that the problem asks for the length of the cable route.

